skills/ is that repository's skills/ folder, unchanged: the three SKILL.md
files (dual-model-harness, subagent-driven-development, writing-plans) and
the four reference notes they name, frontmatter and all.

Rewritten: the packaging. The original is a Hermes Agent plugin -- a Python
register() that walks its own skills/ folder and hands each SKILL.md to the
harness -- and this folder is a Nodecode knowledge cell, whose .asd declares
:properties ((:knowledge . t)) and no component, so the folder is recorded
and never loaded and the index reads the same SKILL.md files in place as
prose skills, listed by their frontmatter name and description and read whole
with (help 'name). The README's table maps the Hermes words the skills use
(delegate_task, todo, read_file, patch) onto Nodecode's own.

Left out: the Python shim and plugin.yaml manifest, which have no Nodecode
equivalent to write; nothing of the prose is dropped, and no script, key or
service came with it. The one thing the skills offer that a knowledge cell
cannot is a runtime hook -- the original registered on import, this folder is
read on demand -- which is why the prose is kept as files rather than
rewritten in Lisp.
